ZAXON WAS ASKED FOR AS A WORKING TOOL AND DOES NOT EXIST (2026-08-04). Zach, dispatching a migration-scoping subagent: 'use zaxon to coordinate'. The only zaxon in the ecosystem is a one-line idea file from 2026-07-29 -- 'an sms/signal/whatsapp/email chatbot version of zach that has his values but can also act as a portal to delegate to agents'. Re-probed: no ~/Documents/Projects/zaxon, no hf7y/zaxon repo, nothing named zaxon on PATH. The subagent was told to coordinate through the channels that do work (read-only scheduler conf inspection; proposing issue bodies back rather than filing them) and to say so. WHY THIS IS WORTH RECORDING RATHER THAN JUST ANSWERING: an idea got referred to in the imperative, as though it were installed. That is the exact direction the ecosystem's own failure record runs -- prose accumulating until it is mistaken for mechanism -- and it is the second instance today (ecosim's sensor still emits CRIT about a dexter relocation that was abandoned). The useful question is not 'build zaxon' but: what job was it being asked to do just now? Reading the request literally, it was DELEGATION COORDINATION -- a place to hand an agent a task and watch it without being at a terminal. GitHub issues already do most of that (bibliothecaire's request/in-progress/delivered queue is exactly this shape and worked unattended tonight), which suggests zaxon's real content is a NOTIFICATION and REPLY surface over a channel Zach already reads on a phone, not a new agent runtime. Filed for the ideate/nightly pass to weigh against the reservoir, not as an approved build.
